    "narrative": "Our strongest play of the day is **Lawrence Butler**, whose score of 74.61 stands alone as our only elite-tier option for this slate. Even with his lineup spot currently pending, the confluence of a favorable park factor, a vulnerable matchup against Zack Littell (4.93 xERA), and a massive platoon edge makes him the engine of our offense today. **Dylan Beavers** (65.38) and **Yainer Diaz** (63.95) also project exceptionally well; **Dylan Beavers** in particular benefits from a high stolen-base environment against the opposing battery, adding vital efficiency in our scarcest category. Meanwhile, **Bryce Harper** (63.62) remains a must-start despite facing a solid arm in Sean Manaea, as a favorable wind forecast and his elite xwOBA profile provide the necessary cushion to justify his presence in the UTIL slot.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s board was keeping **Jung Hoo Lee** (47.73) on the bench. While his score is respectable, he ultimately lost out to the superior platoon and park-adjusted profiles of **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Daulton Varsho**. We are navigating some risk with **Cal Raleigh** (51.36), whose efficiency is suppressed by a difficult matchup against Logan Webb and a negative platoon split. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remaining sidelined on the IL, we are relying on our depth\u2014specifically **Gavin Sheets** and his 63.91 score\u2014to anchor the corner infield spots. We are monitoring the lineups closely for **Lawrence Butler**; should he slide down the order, we may see a slight regression in his scoring output, though his matchup remains the most favorable on the docket for the LawDog squad.",
